From 29e51dcf7da0b42682c64782a7bf7e9e2604c053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:12:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 288: two mentions are enough to break - the smoke failure was
 a real restriction

The smoke fell on the corruption-site guard, and the guard was right about the
count while the restriction behind it was wrong. Requiring three mentions per
address discards most of the tape: the address-holdout run reported nine items
above two mentions on a 104-address tape, and the smoke tape is smaller still.

Two mentions is enough, and the case it unlocks is the one in short supply.
Replacing one of {A, B} gives {A, X} with the original B gone from the visible
evidence - a perfectly formed UNRECOVERABLE example, which is exactly what
G_honest_unrecoverable needs a supply of and what three-mention addresses
produce least often. Three-mention addresses go on providing the recoverable
ones, so the mix improves in both directions rather than merely growing.

The guard now prints what it saw - site count, item count, the histogram of
mentions per address - instead of a bare refusal, and the smoke tape asks for
300 addresses rather than 60 so it exercises the path it is meant to smoke.

The full run already in flight is unaffected in correctness; it simply trains
and scores on the three-mention subset, so its denominators will be small and
its dup counts smaller. Worth rerunning on this once it lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RYDM9MUk761CZjn7SmTaug
